1794959654880528	sippycup-2u2m2v	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-fl0	{"body":"Decision (2026-11-17): drop sipsak and use the in-tree Python OPTIONS transaction (sip_options_preflight) for both the launcher preflight and the campaign options step. Evaluated sipexer v2.1.0 (released 2026-09-17, GPLv3, 12 MB static Go binary, not packaged in Debian trixie; sha256 of the linux-amd64 tarball 42ba5155a16c2070f3a73a9145fadc8df07f7c355cf69312b39fa0a5b220663f). Hands-on in a throwaway container it sent a correct Via with rport, but its exit code is the SIP status mod 256 (200 means success, 153 on timeout, 138 on refused TCP), its TLS verification is all-or-nothing like sipsak's, and it would add an unpackaged pinned binary. It does not fix what is wrong with sipsak; the in-tree transaction already exists, is under test, verifies TLS by default, and removes a dependency plus the --add-host hostname workaround. Not tested for sipexer: TLS, WS/WSS, Digest, -nagios. Follow-up implementation is tracked separately."}	blake3:jF6fdQRE0gn1bDV4ogoS4qr9zB6m1wn_CLcslfIP_Qw
1794959654980685	sippycup-2u2m2v	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2tb	{"description":"Outcome of the bn-fl0 decision: remove sipsak and use the in-tree OPTIONS transaction everywhere.\n\nWork\n- Give sip_options_preflight (lib/sippycup/integration.py) a small in-image command-line entry point: host, port, transport, timeout. Exit 0 on the agreed success contract, 1 for a SIP response outside it, 2 for a transport failure or timeout. Print the status line.\n- Decide and document the success contract. Today any \"SIP/2.0 \" status line passes, including a 500: that is reachability, not health. Recommended: report the status class, treat any final response as reachable, and let callers require 2xx explicitly.\n- Bracket IPv6 literals in Via correctly and read TCP/TLS responses until the header terminator instead of a single recv.\n- Add one bounded UDP retransmission within the existing budget so a single lost datagram is not a failed preflight; count it against the packet ceiling.\n- TLS: verify by default. The launcher preflight currently passes sipsak --tls-ignore-cert-failure; replace that with an explicit, logged opt-out that reports the result as unverified rather than as a pass. Coordinate with the SNI-pinned TLS work (bn-1bi).\n- Switch bin/container-preflight and the options step of bin/campaign-sipp-runner to the entry point; keep the nc and openssl stages.\n- Remove sipsak from the Containerfile, README tool table, doctor inventory, and smoke checks, and remove the --add-host hostname workaround from bin/sippycup if nothing else needs it (check sngrep, SIPp, and PJSUA on the host network first).\n\nAcceptance\n- The practice-target gate passes over UDP, TCP, and TLS with sipsak absent from the image.\n- Exit codes are covered by tests for 200, a 4xx/5xx, timeout, refused TCP, and a TLS name mismatch.\n- No behavior change for campaign execute beyond the retransmission.","kind":"task","labels":["tooling","preflight","tls"],"parent":"bn-za4","size":"s","title":"Replace sipsak with the in-tree OPTIONS transaction"}	blake3:QKChbxN3cw0kS6NNcMe96_Qj1KKGz1pLAaGN-iZYsyI
1794959655007510	sippycup-2u2m2v	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-fl0	{"state":"done"}	blake3:r4_YpmOXg47OOktu1nCIUf8nHtxJAzJNaahJt7PMh-0
1794960668738263	sippycup-2u2m2v	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-39v	{"state":"done"}	blake3:zIlF_EGxDuC4e-IK2PNLlQieIsguR0t8UdxhUG3cYro
1794960668753104	sippycup-2u2m2v	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-39v	{"body":"Merged to main in d4de0d5 (scope init/questions/check/compile, staleness sidecar, advisor integration; 52 tests). Review fixes: generated expectations no longer require DTMF (a baseline call sends none), and source addresses must include the local capture-side address behind NAT. Known limits: the profile carries only the first target; reject destinations get no final-status expectation; a compiled campaign for an account-requiring target still cannot run until bn-1c5 lands."}	blake3:o0EJ4L3LQ-xN5uOG9IsWEhuPAz47e2EgeEdWt2Tfk3E
1794961661314041	sippycup-2u2m2v	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2ky	{"body":"Merged to main in 665f2eb: sippycup call (gate, in-namespace capture, one OPTIONS, one PJSUA call, report/triage/assert, run directory) plus the reusable lib/sippycup_softphone driver. Lead verification: 518 host tests, call-selftest, and the real launcher path against a softphone on the host network (preflight ok, call answered, scope guard hung up because that peer advertised an unlisted media address). Still open before closing: prove Digest registration and TLS against the practice target (bn-yfj)."}	blake3:Zc25S4IIBENzjAtC1ermine1rGhbTRd_t0fOnJqx8IA
