1794967433066594	sippycup-2u2m2v	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-20j	{"body":"Further items from wave-two review: (1) campaign run with secrets drops the OPTIONS step's JSON summary (step.output_truncated, retainedBytes 0) while campaign execute keeps it; (2) the capture watchdog cannot count calls inside TLS, so the calls ceiling is not enforced for TLS campaigns (packet, byte, rate, duration ceilings still are); (3) the softphone runner does not force PJSUA's local RTP port into the authorized media range; (4) no DTMF in the softphone runner; (5) evidence privacy lint flags softphone.log because the redacted Proxy-Authorization header line remains; (6) unused socket/ssl imports in lib/sippycup/integration.py; (7) only TLS 1.2 was exercised by the practice gate."}	blake3:5y6HUhRz6lJ4V7NZpJ_DpnrumUqBOWfKWJRnGeQVAas
1794970128466090	sippycup-2u2m2v	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-19a	{"description":"RFC 4733 DTMF send, SDES-SRTP offer, local RTP port pinned to the authorized range, and the real SIP status on failed registration, in the driver, guided call, and campaign runner. Verified against the practice target.","kind":"task","labels":["live"],"parent":"bn-za4","title":"Softphone features: DTMF, SRTP, local RTP port range, registration status"}	blake3:gxLc_9dvVtakLfP9RUq4-3tfUFrrLynsMADt_K-4KQw
