1795021103950127	sippycup-2u2m2v	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3gi	{"description":"lib/sippycup_oracle/adapter.py _sip/_sdp use _scalar, which takes the first list item; with tshark --no-duplicate-keys a TCP segment holding two SIP messages loses the second, so dialog reconstruction can miss e.g. a 200 OK coalesced with a 180. Found by the ladder builder, who iterates layers itself. Also: _ws.malformed from an invalid a=crypto base64 marks the whole frame MALFORMED.","kind":"bug","parent":"bn-32q","size":"s","title":"Oracle adapter reads only the first SIP message when one TCP frame carries several"}	blake3:1fvAfNIJ8aE1_Pz0ZCrNNGz78qX8CkQ-nXTyU5ywRTo
