1795034778352758	bob-dev	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-2ap	{"link_type":"related_to","target":"bn-1xm"}	blake3:A1UptWxdSP8U1_-DfUeuhQItPeJyYAQP0rAmCHUSu5g
1795034778372046	bob-dev	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-3f0	{"link_type":"related_to","target":"bn-6zn"}	blake3:3ktLTcjE-xVJH-P0YBjiwRR778uUqtUdLWtxyeZzVfw
1795034778391332	bob-dev	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-24x	{"field":"parent","value":"bn-3f0"}	blake3:vfHbND4VKwQkWtJNedW2KdEgDb0HNekitL85dwEUmio
1795034778409943	bob-dev	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-24x	{"field":"description","value":"Problem\n-------\nlib/sippycup/campaign.py:1269-1288 derives the capture filter from the signaling host only, and lib/sippycup/runtime.py:766/1063 requires the plan filter to equal it. The campaign softphone runner, however, admits media from any address in authorization.networks (lib/sippycup_softphone/campaign_runner.py:224) and from the step's frozen signaling addresses. In the proxy/SBC shape the practice target documents (signaling on 127.0.0.3, media on 127.0.0.2), RTP from the media address is allowed by the runner but invisible to capture, the packet watchdog, and the byte ceiling. The docs' claim that all media stays inside the capture filter is therefore false for split media.\n\nThis is an equivalent-path inconsistency: the guided call, matrix, and checks honor the profile's media.networks, while the campaign planner captures only signaling target addresses plus the media port range.\n\nOutcome\n-------\n- Add a media-only network allowlist to the campaign plan (for example authorization.mediaNetworks) and use it for the capture filter and packet watchdog. Do not widen authorization.networks for signaling merely to make capture work.\n- Allow the softphone runner to accept a media peer only from the frozen signaling addresses or the media-only networks, and require its port to stay in authorization.mediaPorts.\n- Include the media networks in the plan digest and re-run the minimal-filter check in runtime.validate_plan.\n- Keep old frozen plans valid: absent mediaNetworks means the old behavior plus a documented limitation; new plans that declare split media must capture it.\n- Add an exit-gate case using the practice proxy: signaling on the proxy, media on 127.0.0.2, capture proves RTP in both directions, and the watchdog counts those packets.\n\nAcceptance criteria\n-------------------\n- A campaign planned against the practice proxy captures RTP from the media address, not just the signaling address.\n- The packet and byte ceilings include captured media packets; a plan that exceeds the ceiling stops before the next step.\n- An out-of-scope media peer is still refused; a media-only network never authorizes signaling.\n- Old plan fixtures remain byte-valid; new fields are optional and versioned.\n- Tests, docs (CAMPAIGN-MANIFEST, PRACTICE-TARGET), and a release gate.\n\nRelates to the campaign capability contract: both must agree on what \"media in scope\" means."}	blake3:xb73vCs_yMCljPsa26ZonrqmYxbMr2GyTMvEoz4Wa4w
1795034787626396	bob-dev	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2cj	{"description":"Problem\n-------\nThe destination model knows only echo, agent, or reject. Scope intake does not ask for feature codes, menus, voicemail boxes, conference rooms, prompts, or PIN refs. The practice Asterisk image deliberately omits app_voicemail, app_confbridge, app_queue, app_directory, res_musiconhold, and app_record, so none of the application features a phone media server actually sells can be rehearsed offline.\n\nOutcome\n-------\n- Extend the practice Asterisk build with app_voicemail, app_confbridge, app_queue, app_directory, res_musiconhold, and app_record, or add a separate loopback-only feature fixture. Add destinations for a simple IVR menu, voicemail deposit/retrieval, a conference room, music on hold, and recording. Generate deterministic per-up mailbox and conference PINs in tmpfs; use canary prompts only.\n- Add an owner-approved features section to scope intake: feature id, dial string, DTMF sequence or secret DTMF ref, expected outcome (menu, mailbox, conference, prompt, recording), canary prompt expectation, max attempts, and lockout note.\n- Add a bounded features plan/run path (or a reviewed campaign case type) that dials one feature, sends only the approved DTMF, records prompt hash/duration and DTMF count, and analyzes the canary. Test with and without the secret PIN and, when approved, from a second identity/tenant.\n- No real mailbox, recording, or user data. No PIN in the plan or artifacts.\n\nAcceptance criteria\n-------------------\n- A practice gate covers IVR menu, voicemail deposit/retrieval, conference join/reject, music-on-hold transition, and recording canary.\n- A feature case cannot pass if the prompt canary or the expected DTMF path was not observed.\n- Secret DTMF never appears in a plan, log, result, journal, or evidence manifest.\n- Cross-account voicemail/conference access is refused unless the identity relationship is approved.\n- Docs: SCOPE-INTAKE, PRACTICE-TARGET, GUIDED-CALL, and the feature schema.\n\nDependencies\n------------\nNeeds A6 (secret DTMF). Cross-account cases also need A5 (identity/tenant model). Relates to bn-yfj (practice target).\n\nGuardrails\n----------\nDo not probe real mailboxes or rooms without owner approval. Do not enumerate PINs. Do not retain prompt audio by default.","kind":"task","labels":["ivr","voicemail","conference","practice","app"],"parent":"bn-2ap","size":"l","title":"Add IVR, voicemail, and conference feature playbooks and practice destinations"}	blake3:NVUNql3rVw_nZaeVuSoDMlvJ3Db01tKxORD_1OHi2Bg
